        ":question/id": "1a1fe1df-e314-527e-a884-f0c092b97472",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-42090",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
